capability xml/copy  an independent copy of a tree
  heroes  built-in `=`
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Node.cloneNode, Document.importNode, copy.deepcopy of an Element
  note    every value of the language is an independent copy (spec section 3)

capability xml/equal  whether two trees are the same
  heroes  built-in `==`
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Node.isSameNode
  note    structural equality; values have no identity, so minidom's isSameNode has no counterpart. It follows the nesting, hence `DEFAULT_MAX_DEPTH`

dropped
  go      CopyToken's buffers aside, Escape: kept for Go 1.0, and EscapeText does the same
  go      Decoder.Strict, Decoder.AutoClose: HTML leniency, refused in xml/html
  python  ElementPath: the module behind find, not in `__all__`; its paths stand in xml/path and xml/xpath
  python  iselement: a question the type answers
  python  ParseError (its `args`, `with_traceback`, `add_note`): what every Python exception has
  python  minidom Node's node-type constants, DOMImplementation, DOMImplementationLS, DocumentLS, getDOMImplementation, Node.getInterface, Node.isSupported, Node.getUserData, Node.setUserData, Node.unlink, TypeInfo, Element.schemaType, Attr.schemaType, Attr.isId, Attr.specified, Element.setIdAttribute, Element.setIdAttributeNS, Element.setIdAttributeNode, Text.isWhitespaceInElementContent, Document.load, Document.loadXML, Document.saveXML, Document.abort, Document.async_, Document.documentURI, Document.errorHandler, Document.strictErrorChecking, Document.implementation: the DOM's interfaces, not a capability (the task's ruling)
  python  minidom NodeList, EmptyNodeList, NamedNodeMap, AttributeList, ReadOnlySequentialNamedNodeMap, Childless, Identified, ElementInfo, StringTypes, defproperty, domreg: the DOM's plumbing
  python  CharacterData.appendData, insertData, deleteData, replaceData, substringData, length, Text.splitText, Text.replaceWholeText: an edit of a text is an edit of a `str`, the work of `strings`

